/P 123 0 R
/T (Where will the new high school be built?)
/E (Where will the new high school be built?)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
159 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 123 0 R
/E (The proposed site for the new high school is the town-owned parcels on Brookfield Street. This site is best known as the location for the Wapping Fair. Plans are underway to move the John J. Mitchell Fairgrounds and associated activities to the town-owned Priest Farm.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
160 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 123 0 R
/T (Were any other sites considered?)
/E (Were any other sites considered?)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
161 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 123 0 R
/E (Yes. The Town evaluated eight other properties with sufficient acreage for a large, comprehensive high school \(approximately 60 acres\). After a thorough review, the fairgrounds property emerged as the most viable option. Other properties were ruled out for one or more of the following reasons: wetlands, topography, acreage, cost, location, environmental factors, or zoning regulations.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
