216 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 125 0 R
/E (Recent proposals for a new Parks & Recreation facility carried substantial price tags ranging from $50 million to $80 million. Repurposing the existing high school provides an opportunity to meet those needs while avoiding the significant cost of constructing a new building.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
217 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 125 0 R
/E (The existing high school is an ideal location for Parks & Recreation, with convenient access to recreational spaces such as Nevers Park, the Community Center, the Farmers Market, the Rotary Pavilion and the Splash Pad. The building itself provides Parks & Recreation the space to expand existing programs and introduce new opportunities for residents of all ages. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
218 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 125 0 R
/E (The benefits extend well beyond Parks & Recreation. The facility could accommodate other town offices and community meetings. Specifically, the Town plans to move offices for Youth & Family Services as well as the Teen Center to the repurposed high school. This will free up much needed space for the seniors at the Community Center. As a supplement to the Community Center, seniors could also make use of valuable specialty spaces already in place, including the pickleball courts, auditorium, cafeteria, art rooms, culinary labs, and gymnasiums. South Windsor can give an existing community asset a new purpose, while avoiding substantial cost to taxpayers.  )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
